{"id":"mahabharata-12-207","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":207,"title":"सप्ताधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 207 · The means: steady practice","summary":{"en":"The teacher gives the means to the goal by the eye of scripture, describing how the one who lives with right conduct reaches the world of Brahma and the middling one the gods. He describes the channels in the body and the way a yogin leaves it at death.","kn":"ಶಾಸ್ತ್ರ ದೃಷ್ಟಿಯಿಂದ ಗುರಿಯ ಉಪಾಯವನ್ನು ಗುರು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಸರಿಯಾದ ನಡತೆಯವನು ಬ್ರಹ್ಮಲೋಕ, ಮಧ್ಯಮನು ದೇವತೆಗಳನ್ನು ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದೇಹದ ನಾಡಿಗಳನ್ನು ಮತ್ತು ಯೋಗಿ ಮರಣದಲ್ಲಿ ದೇಹ ಬಿಡುವ ಬಗೆಯನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"गुरु शास्त्र-दृष्टि से लक्ष्य का उपाय बताते हैं कि सम्यक् आचरण वाला ब्रह्मलोक और मध्यम देवताओं को पाता है। वे देह की नाड़ियों और मृत्यु पर योगी के देह छोड़ने की रीति का वर्णन करते हैं।","te":"గురువు శాస్త్ర దృష్టితో లక్ష్యానికి ఉపాయాన్ని చెబుతాడు; సరైన ప్రవర్తన గలవాడు బ్రహ్మలోకం, మధ్యముడు దేవతలను పొందుతాడు. దేహంలోని నాడులను, మరణంలో యోగి దేహం విడిచే తీరును వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"நூற்பார்வையில் குறிக்கோளை அடையும் வழியைக் குரு கூறுகிறார்; நல்லொழுக்கமுடையவன் பிரம்மலோகத்தையும் நடுத்தரன் தேவரையும் அடைகிறான். உடலின் நாடிகளையும் யோகி இறக்கும்போது உடலை விடும் விதத்தையும் விவரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"ശാസ്ത്രത്തിന്റെ കണ്ണിലൂടെ ലക്ഷ്യത്തിലേക്കുള്ള മാർഗ്ഗം ഗുരു നൽകുന്നു; നല്ല നടപ്പിൽ ജീവിക്കുന്നവൻ ബ്രഹ്മലോകത്തിലും, മധ്യമനായവൻ ദേവലോകത്തിലും എത്തുമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു. ശരീരത്തിലെ നാഡികളെയും, മരണസമയത്ത് യോഗി ശരീരം വിടുന്ന വഴിയെയും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.207; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"गुरुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The teacher said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अत्रोपायं प्रवक्ष्यामि यथावच्छास्त्रचक्षुषा ।\nतद्विज्ञानाच्चरन्प्राज्ञः प्राप्नुयात्परमां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here I will explain the means, as seen through the eye of scripture; knowing it and living by it, the wise reach the highest goal."}},{"n":2,"text":"सर्वेषामेव भूतानां पुरुषः श्रेष्ठ उच्यते ।\nपुरुषेभ्यो द्विजानाहुर्द्विजेभ्यो मन्त्रवादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among all beings, the human is called best; among humans, the twice-born; and among the twice-born, those who speak the mantras."}},{"n":3,"text":"सर्वभूतविशिष्टास्ते सर्वज्ञाः सर्वदर्शिनः ।\nब्राह्मणा वेदतत्त्वज्ञास्तत्त्वार्थगतिनिश्चयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These are the foremost of all beings, all-knowing and all-seeing: the Brahmanas, who know the essence of the Veda and are sure of the way to the true meaning."}},{"n":4,"text":"नेत्रहीनो यथा ह्येकः कृच्छ्राणि लभतेऽध्वनि ।\nज्ञानहीनस्तथा लोके तस्माज्ज्ञानविदोऽधिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a blind man alone on a road meets hardship, so does one without knowledge in the world; therefore those who know are greater."}},{"n":5,"text":"तांस्तानुपासते धर्मान्धर्मकामा यथागमम् ।\nन त्वेषामर्थसामान्यमन्तरेण गुणानिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who love dharma follow those various duties according to scripture; yet without these virtues they do not reach the common aim."}},{"n":6,"text":"वाग्देहमनसां शौचं क्षमा सत्यं धृतिः स्मृतिः ।\nसर्वधर्मेषु धर्मज्ञा ज्ञापयन्ति गुणानिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Purity of speech, body and mind, patience, truth, steadiness and memory: those who know dharma teach these virtues in all duties."}},{"n":7,"text":"यदिदं ब्रह्मणो रूपं ब्रह्मचर्यमिति स्मृतम् ।\nपरं तत्सर्वभूतेभ्यस्तेन यान्ति परां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This form of Brahman that is called brahmacharya is supreme above all beings; by it people reach the highest goal."}},{"n":8,"text":"लिङ्गसंयोगहीनं यच्छरीरस्पर्शवर्जितम् ।\nश्रोत्रेण श्रवणं चैव चक्षुषा चैव दर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is free from union of the sexual organs and from touching bodies; and from hearing with the ear and seeing with the eye,"}},{"n":9,"text":"जिह्वया रसनं यच्च तदेव परिवर्जितम् ।\nबुद्ध्या च व्यवसायेन ब्रह्मचर्यमकल्मषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and tasting with the tongue: that too is given up. With the resolve of understanding, brahmacharya is without stain."}},{"n":10,"text":"सम्यग्वृत्तिर्ब्रह्मलोकं प्राप्नुयान्मध्यमः सुरान् ।\nद्विजाग्र्यो जायते विद्वान्कन्यसीं वृत्तिमास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One of right conduct reaches the world of Brahma; the middling reaches the gods; one who follows the lowest course is born a learned best of the twice-born."}},{"n":11,"text":"सुदुष्करं ब्रह्मचर्यमुपायं तत्र मे शृणु ।\nसंप्रवृत्तमुदीर्णं च निगृह्णीयाद्द्विजो मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmacharya is very hard; hear from me the means. The twice-born should restrain the mind when it has arisen and surges up."}},{"n":12,"text":"योषितां न कथाः श्राव्या न निरीक्ष्या निरम्बराः ।\nकदाचिद्दर्शनादासां दुर्बलानाविशेद्रजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Talk about women should not be listened to, nor should they be looked at unclothed; at times the sight of them can stir passion in the weak."}},{"n":13,"text":"रागोत्पत्तौ चरेत्कृच्छ्रमह्नस्त्रिः प्रविशेदपः ।\nमग्नः स्वप्ने च मनसा त्रिर्जपेदघमर्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When desire arises one should do hard penance, enter water three times a day, and in a dream, plunged in water, recite the Aghamarshana three times in the mind."}},{"n":14,"text":"पाप्मानं निर्दहेदेवमन्तर्भूतं रजोमयम् ।\nज्ञानयुक्तेन मनसा संततेन विचक्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this way the wise man should burn away the sin of rajas that lies within, with a mind steadily joined to knowledge."}},{"n":15,"text":"कुणपामेध्यसंयुक्तं यद्वदच्छिद्रबन्धनम् ।\nतद्वद्देहगतं विद्यादात्मानं देहबन्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a flawless bond joined with corpse and filth, so know the self in the body to be bound by the body."}},{"n":16,"text":"वातपित्तकफान्रक्तं त्वङ्मांसं स्नायुमस्थि च ।\nमज्जां चैव सिराजालैस्तर्पयन्ति रसा नृणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fluids feed in men the wind, bile and phlegm, the blood, skin, flesh, sinews, bone and marrow, through networks of vessels."}},{"n":17,"text":"दश विद्याद्धमन्योऽत्र पञ्चेन्द्रियगुणावहाः ।\nयाभिः सूक्ष्माः प्रतायन्ते धमन्योऽन्याः सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know there to be ten channels that carry the qualities of the five senses, from which thousands of other fine channels spread."}},{"n":18,"text":"एवमेताः सिरानद्यो रसोदा देहसागरम् ।\nतर्पयन्ति यथाकालमापगा इव सागरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So these river-like vessels carry fluid into the sea of the body at the proper time, as rivers feed the sea."}},{"n":19,"text":"मध्ये च हृदयस्यैका सिरा त्वत्र मनोवहा ।\nशुक्रं संकल्पजं नॄणां सर्वगात्रैर्विमुञ्चति ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the middle of the heart is one vessel that carries the mind; from it, semen born of thought is released through all the limbs of men."}},{"n":20,"text":"सर्वगात्रप्रतायिन्यस्तस्या ह्यनुगताः सिराः ।\nनेत्रयोः प्रतिपद्यन्ते वहन्त्यस्तैजसं गुणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The vessels spreading through all the limbs follow it and reach the two eyes, carrying the quality of light."}},{"n":21,"text":"पयस्यन्तर्हितं सर्पिर्यद्वन्निर्मथ्यते खजैः ।\nशुक्रं निर्मथ्यते तद्वद्देहसंकल्पजैः खजैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As ghee hidden in milk is churned out by the churning-sticks, so semen is churned out by the stirrings born of the body's thoughts."}},{"n":22,"text":"स्वप्नेऽप्येवं यथाभ्येति मनःसंकल्पजं रजः ।\nशुक्रमस्पर्शजं देहात्सृजन्त्यस्य मनोवहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"So in dream too, the passion born of the mind's thought comes; the mind-carrying vessels release semen from his body without any touch."}},{"n":23,"text":"महर्षिर्भगवानत्रिर्वेद तच्छुक्रसंभवम् ।\nत्रिबीजमिन्द्रदैवत्यं तस्मादिन्द्रियमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great sage, the lord Atri, knows how that semen comes to be; it has three seeds and Indra as its deity, so it is called indriya."}},{"n":24,"text":"ये वै शुक्रगतिं विद्युर्भूतसंकरकारिकाम् ।\nविरागा दग्धदोषास्ते नाप्नुयुर्देहसंभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who know the course of semen, which causes the mixing of beings, become dispassionate with their faults burnt away, and do not take birth in a body."}},{"n":25,"text":"गुणानां साम्यमागम्य मनसैव मनोवहम् ।\nदेहकर्म नुदन्प्राणानन्तकाले विमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the evenness of the qualities, driving the mind-carrier by the mind alone, and pushing away the body's actions and breaths, one is freed at the end of time."}},{"n":26,"text":"भविता मनसो ज्ञानं मन एव प्रतायते ।\nज्योतिष्मद्विरजो दिव्यमत्र सिद्धं महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowledge will arise from the mind, and the mind itself expands; here the luminous, passionless, divine state is attained by the great-souled."}},{"n":27,"text":"तस्मात्तदविघाताय कर्म कुर्यादकल्मषम् ।\nरजस्तमश्च हित्वेह न तिर्यग्गतिमाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, to keep it unhindered, one should do stainless work; having given up rajas and tamas here, one does not reach an animal birth."}},{"n":28,"text":"तरुणाधिगतं ज्ञानं जरादुर्बलतां गतम् ।\nपरिपक्वबुद्धिः कालेन आदत्ते मानसं बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowledge gained in youth, though weakened by old age, is taken up by one of ripened understanding in time as strength of mind."}},{"n":29,"text":"सुदुर्गमिव पन्थानमतीत्य गुणबन्धनम् ।\nयदा पश्येत्तदा दोषानतीत्यामृतमश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having crossed the bond of the qualities, like a very hard road, when one sees thus, then, passing beyond faults, one enjoys immortality."}}]}]}